{title: Living Hope}
{subtitle: Romans 15:13; 1 Peter 1:3; 1 Corinthians 15:55–57; Isaiah 40:31}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bbmaj7/D] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Bbmaj7/D] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
There's an [Bb]empty chair beside me and the [Gm]evening light is thin
I [Eb]have held a hand grown cold now, I have [F]let the silence in
But I have [Bb]not been left with nothing, though my [Gm]eyes are wet with grief
There's [Eb]a word that holds me steady like an [F]anchor underneath
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
May the [Gm]God of [Eb]hope fill you with [Bb]all joy and [F]peace
As you [Gm]trust in [Eb]him
So [Bb]that you may over[F]flow with hope
By [Eb]the power of the Holy Spir[Bb]it [Bbmaj7/D][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Blessed be the God and Father [Gm]of our Lord Jesus Christ
In [Eb]his great mercy he has given us new birth [F]into a living hope
[Bb]Through the resurrection of Jesus [F/A][Gm]Christ from the dead
The [Eb]stone is rolled away, and the morn[F]ing light has come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
May the [Gm]God of [Eb]hope fill you with [Bb]all joy and [F]peace
As you [Gm]trust in [Eb]him
So [Bb]that you may over[F]flow with hope
By [Eb]the power of the Holy Spir[Bb]it
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Where, O death, is your [Bb]vic[F]tory
[Eb]Where, O death, is [Gm]your [F]sting
[Eb]But thanks be to God, who [Gm]gives us the [F]victory
[Eb]Through our Lord Jesus Christ
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Those who hope in the LORD [Gm]will renew their strength
[Eb]They will rise on wings [Bb]like ea[F]gles
[Bb]They will run and not grow [Gm]weary
[Eb]They will walk and not be [Bb]faint
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
So that [Eb]you may overflow with hope
A living hope
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
